IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 3 (ss 13 to 18):
-- additional consumer rights in respect of non-conforming goods.
-- Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 1006 to 1301.
--
-- Whether a person "deals as consumer" (Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977, Part 1),
-- what is a contract of sale of goods, a contract for the transfer of goods or a
-- hire-purchase agreement, and what terms sections 13 to 15 of the Sale of Goods Act
-- 1979, 3 to 5 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982 and 6A to 6C of the Hire-Purchase
-- Act 1969 imply, are the answers of those Acts and are facts here.

§ `Part 3 -- Additional consumer rights in respect of non-conforming goods`

§§ `13. Interpretation of this Part`

-- 13(2) and (3): "dealing as consumer" is the Unfair Contract Terms Act's; a
-- transferor who claims that the transferee does not deal as consumer must show it.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 13(2) and (3)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee deals as consumer for the purposes of this Part` IF
    IF g's `the transferor claims that the transferee does not deal as consumer`
    THEN NOT g's `the transferor has shown that the transferee does not deal as consumer`
    ELSE g's `the transferee deals as consumer under Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 13(4)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` IF
        g's `there is a breach of an express term of the contract in relation to the goods`
     OR (CONSIDER g's `kind of contract`
         WHEN `a contract of sale of goods` THEN
             g's `there is a breach of a term implied by section 13, 14 or 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979`
         WHEN `a contract for the transfer of goods` THEN
             g's `there is a breach of a term implied by section 3, 4 or 5 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982`
         WHEN `a hire-purchase agreement` THEN
             g's `there is a breach of a term implied by section 6A, 6B or 6C of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969`)

-- 13(5): the definitions of "consumer" and "goods" in s 2(1), s 2(2) and Part 4 do
-- not apply to this Part.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 13(5)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN `the provision is the definition of consumer or goods in section 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is section 2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is in Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies to this Part` IF
        NOT `the provision is the definition of consumer or goods in section 2(1)`
    AND NOT `the provision is section 2(2)`
    AND NOT `the provision is in Part 4`

§§ `14. Application of this Part`

-- 14(3) and (4): goods that do not conform at any time within the 6 months
-- starting after the date of delivery are taken not to have conformed at delivery,
-- unless it is established that they did, or the presumption is incompatible with
-- the nature of the goods or of the lack of conformity.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 14(3)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` IF
    CONSIDER g's `the date on which the lack of conformity appeared`
    WHEN JUST appeared THEN
            appeared GREATER THAN g's `the goods were delivered on`
        AND appeared AT MOST `add months` (g's `the goods were delivered on`) 6
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 14(3) and (4)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are taken not to have conformed at the date of delivery` IF
        `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` g
    AND NOT g's `it is established that the goods did conform at the date of delivery`
    AND NOT g's `applying the presumption is incompatible with the nature of the goods or the nature of the lack of conformity`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 14(1)(b)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract at the time of delivery` IF
        `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` g
    AND (   g's `the lack of conformity is shown to have existed at the time of delivery`
         OR `the goods are taken not to have conformed at the date of delivery` g)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 14(1)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Part applies` IF
        `the transferee deals as consumer for the purposes of this Part` g
    AND `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract at the time of delivery` g
    AND g's `the contract was made on` AT LEAST YMD 2012 9 1

§§ `15. Repair or replacement of goods`

-- 15(3): the transferee must not require the remedy if it is impossible, or
-- disproportionate in comparison to the other remedy, or disproportionate in
-- comparison to an appropriate reduction or rescission.  15(4) says when one remedy
-- is disproportionate; the two disproportion facts record that finding.  15(5), that
-- reasonable time and significant inconvenience are judged by the nature of the
-- goods and the purpose for which they were acquired, guides the finding and is inert.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(3)(a), (b) and (c) and s 15(4)"
GIVEN r IS A `Remedy Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee may require the remedy` IF
        NOT r's `the remedy is impossible`
    AND NOT r's `the remedy imposes on the transferor costs that are unreasonable in comparison with those imposed by the other remedy, taking into account the value the goods would have if they conformed, the significance of the lack of conformity and whether the other remedy could be effected without significant inconvenience`
    AND NOT r's `the remedy imposes on the transferor costs that are unreasonable in comparison with those imposed by an appropriate reduction in the amount to be paid or by rescission, taking into account the same three matters`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(1)(a) and (b) and s 15(3)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
      c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee may require the transferor to repair the goods` IF
        `this Part applies` g
    AND `the transferee may require the remedy` (c's `facts of repair`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(1)(a) and (b) and s 15(3)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
      c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee may require the transferor to replace the goods` IF
        `this Part applies` g
    AND `the transferee may require the remedy` (c's `facts of replacement`)

-- 15(2): once a remedy is required the transferor must repair or replace within a
-- reasonable time and without significant inconvenience, and bear the necessary costs.
-- Time and inconvenience are matters of judgement (15(5)); the finding is a fact.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(2)(a)"
GIVEN c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferor has met the requirement of section 15(2)(a)` IF
        NOT c's `the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace`
     OR c's `the transferor repaired or replaced the goods within a reasonable time and without causing significant inconvenience to the transferee`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(2)(b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferor must bear the necessary costs of the repair or replacement` IF
    c's `the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace`

§§ `16. Reduction in amount to be paid or rescission of contract`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 16(2)(a)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
      c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee may require neither repair nor replacement` IF
        NOT `the transferee may require the remedy` (c's `facts of repair`)
    AND NOT `the transferee may require the remedy` (c's `facts of replacement`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 16(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
      c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition in section 16(2) is satisfied` IF
        `the transferee may require neither repair nor replacement` g c
     OR (    c's `the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace`
         AND NOT `the transferor has met the requirement of section 15(2)(a)` c)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 16(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN g IS A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
      c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee may require a reduction in the amount to be paid or rescind the contract` IF
        `this Part applies` g
    AND `the condition in section 16(2) is satisfied` g c

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 16(3) and s 18(5)"
GIVEN `the transferee rescinds the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee has had use of the goods since they were delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reimbursement may be reduced to take account of the use the transferee has had of the goods` IF
        `the transferee rescinds the contract`
    AND `the transferee has had use of the goods since they were delivered`

§§ `17. Relation to other remedies, etc.`

-- 17(1) read with 17(2): after requiring repair or replacement, the transferee must
-- not reject and terminate, or require the goods to be repaired or replaced, until the
-- transferor has had a reasonable time.  As printed, 17(2)(b) covers "requires the
-- goods to be repaired or replaced, as the case may be", which would catch the very
-- requirement that 17(1) presupposes; the rule reads it as a further requirement of
-- the other remedy (NOTES.md F2).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 17(1) and (2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Remedy Claim Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` IF
        c's `the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace`
    AND (   c's `the transferee rejects the goods and terminates the contract for breach of condition`
         OR c's `the transferee, having required repair or replacement, further requires the goods to be repaired or replaced by the other remedy`)
    AND NOT c's `the transferee has given the transferor a reasonable time in which to repair or replace`

§§ `18. Powers of court`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 18(1) and (2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Court Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order specific performance of an obligation under section 15` IF
        p's `proceedings in which a remedy is sought under Part 3`
    AND p's `the transferee applies for specific performance of an obligation imposed on the transferor by section 15`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 18(3) and (4)"
GIVEN p IS A `Court Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may proceed as if the transferee had required the other remedy` IF
        p's `proceedings in which a remedy is sought under Part 3`
    AND p's `the transferee requires the transferor to give effect to a remedy under section 15 or 16, or claims to rescind under section 16`
    AND p's `the court decides that another remedy under section 15 or 16 is appropriate`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 18(5)"
GIVEN p IS A `Court Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order that the reimbursement be reduced to take account of the use` IF
        p's `proceedings in which a remedy is sought under Part 3`
    AND p's `the transferee has claimed to rescind the contract`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 18(7)"
GIVEN p IS A `Court Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Small Claims Tribunal may act under section 18` IF
    p's `the tribunal is a Small Claims Tribunal acting within its jurisdiction under section 5 of the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984`

-- 18(6): the court may make an order unconditionally or on terms as to damages,
-- payment for the goods and otherwise as it thinks just: a grant of discretion
-- without a condition, so inert.
